            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Please write a commit message, specifically try to articulate why this is useful.  It's known that sd_bus supports it, but generally i would expect that you'd want to associate this with an actual destroy/reconnect of the connection itself."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gustav Lindberg",
                        "email": "gustali@axis.com",
                        "username": "GustavLindberg99"
                    },
                    "message": "Added an explanation. If you want a higher level wrapper instead (like `start_shutdown()` and `ready_to_shut_down()` methods) let me know. What's important is that `sd_bus_release_name_async()` can be called somewhere to avoid race conditions with systemd."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "It looks like you're new.  Thank you for the patch!\n\nWe have our contributing guide documented here.  You'll likely need to execute one of the CLAs that are available before we can merge this.  If your company already has a CLA, please make sure the CLA manager adds you to the list of approved contributors."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gustav Lindberg",
                        "email": "gustali@axis.com",
                        "username": "GustavLindberg99"
                    },
                    "message": "I've asked our contract manager to take care of this, and she says it's complicated and will take some time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "\ud83d\udc4d Let us know if there's anything we can do to help."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gustav Lindberg",
                        "email": "gustali@axis.com",
                        "username": "GustavLindberg99"
                    },
                    "message": "From what I understand the problem is that our company is owned by Canon, and your CLA has some sort of \"affiliates\" part requiring us to sign it on behalf of Canon, which we cannot do. Our legal team is wondering if you can remove this \"affiliates\" so that we can sign the agreement without involving any other companies?\n\nIt might also be easier of our legal team could contact you directly, what would be the best way of doing that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a standard form from Linux Foundation.  We cannot change it.  If there are concerns with it from your company we'll have to email the CLA coordinator for LF: manager@lfprojects.org."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/bus.hpp",
                    "line": 597,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We generally don't want to hold state like this within the connection object itself.  Normally you would pass this by std::move into your various handlers in case this call is done multiple times in a row before the first callback succeeds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/bus.hpp",
                    "line": 597,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gustav Lindberg",
                        "email": "gustali@axis.com",
                        "username": "GustavLindberg99"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
